       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 to 2,550 mg/day for extended-release. This order is double that limit. It carries a high risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release. It may be what you meant if \"1700\" was a typo.\n- **1,700 mg/day divided**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **Another dose.** If so, please give me the dose and frequency.\n\nIf you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give the clinical reason. I'll add that to the order note. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
