       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your reason for the dose is about timing, not about what the patient needs. At 5,100 mg/day, the order could seriously harm the patient with lactic acidosis or severe GI toxicity, and no schedule makes that safe.\n\nHere is what I can do right away:\n- **Enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is the maximum standard dose, 2,550 mg/day.\n- **Enter a lower starting dose and titrate**, for example 500 mg twice daily or 850 mg once daily, if the patient is new to metformin.\n- **Add a note asking for pharmacy or attending review.** If there is a clinical reason for the higher dose that I don't know about, that review can approve it and enter it.\n\nTell me which one you want and I'll enter it now. That should still let you settle the plan before evening rounds."
